{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/workroom as main carries it, at merge commit 8f0b86f30644ca9e2b1fc0e54a8958a237a221b8, which landed the report-lifecycle validation approved by codex in 5975a2f1 and ratified in b1aa259f. (Records are named here by the trailing eight hex of their event id.)\n\nWhat the merge changed here is one addition to kinds.go: StarterLifecycle(kind) returns the lifecycle a compatibility-catalog kind carries, and whether the kind is in that catalog at all, without constructing a projection first. It exists so the write path in internal/app can tell whether an act is a report before it has a snapshot to consult. Callers still need the active vocabulary for declared kinds, and the comment on the function says so, because the starter catalog is a compatibility floor and not the vocabulary.\n\nNothing else in this package changed, and the fold's own report-lifecycle rules are untouched. The refusal added in this merge sits in front of the fold, not inside it.\n\nGates run at this exact merge commit in the main checkout: go vet ./..., go build ./..., go test ./internal/... -count=1, with internal/docset run on its own rather than concurrently with another suite.\n\nSuccession is incomplete here, for two separate reasons, and both are worth stating plainly.\n\nSix live artifacts sit at this path. I retired one, 7feed9e4, which I authored and no page cites. Three others — 24279d39, 16dac6fa and 0e36d503 — were recorded by codex; the fold admits a supersession only from the target's author or from an actor holding ratifier, and claude is a bare participant, so codex or hugh has to retire those.\n\nThe remaining two are mine but must stay live for now. 0d7b8dde is cited by eleven pages — docs/README.md, docs/anchoring.md, docs/concepts/components.md, docs/concepts/staleness.md, docs/how-to/end-to-end.md, docs/reference/architecture.md, docs/reference/gs/merge.md, docs/reference/gs/status.md, docs/reference/gs/supersede.md, docs/reference/mcp/supersede.md and docs/why.md — and b67e9b56 is cited by docs/concepts/work-loop.md. Retiring either would leave those pages resting on a withdrawn record and take the docset gate red. Re-anchoring them onto this record and then retiring both is ordinary implementing work needing its own request. Until then this path carries several live artifacts and a reader should treat this one as what main carries.\n\nIt rests on 3b7f205d at cmd/gs (event sha 24d800c0ea95157cd7464d1281f4b3f83b7f205d), live and not stale, and not on any record this merge retires or on the review of the merged head.","body":{"commit":"8f0b86f30644ca9e2b1fc0e54a8958a237a221b8","path":"internal/workroom"}}